A||||2||Rodney||New front hood gas struts||||1||
Z||000000||Rodney||07-27-2001||09:02 AM||||I have been working on a front gas hood strut to replace the OEM ratchet device. I have tried some variations and have settled on my latest design. It replaces the front ratchet assembly and opens the hood as far as the top setting of the OEM assembly. It will not lift your hood. You still have to lift the hood all the way but it holds the front hood open well and is strong enough to keep it up in the wind and inclines. Price will be $69 and $8.00 shipping. I should have some finished in a week or so. Not on my web page yet. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Loki||07-27-2001||10:39 AM||||HEy Rodney, have you thought about making some that go down near the radiator and lift there? I have seen a few with them and seems to work well...  Just a thought.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodney||07-27-2001||04:51 PM||||One guy I talked to that did it that way said his hood started to warp from the pressure of the struts. Another one who did it almost the same way said his hood would not open when the radiator was hot. Said the struts would lock up until they cooled. So I'm going with this design. Easy to install and it uses a very light pressure strut eliminating any warping problems. ||||reg||1
